The problem with that is that fancy graphics make it harder for 
maintainers to add more gameplay.  Would anyone have added the Tourist 
class to Nethack is they had to make a full set of 3D models for it and 
the 100s (literally) of actions that a NH character can perform?  No, of 
course they wouldn't.  Would nethack.alt.org be the centrer-of-community 
that it is today if people couldn't play via telnet?  No, it wouldn't.

Anything graphical will most likely be obsolete in a few years, but 
text-mode games can persist.  NH itself represents a fairly smooth 
development from the original Rogue, which means it has been around 
longer than I have (or you I suspect).

Of course, it will never again be fully mainstream ...

